  "slug": "colored-indexes-832d",
  "summary": "Seven preprints and papers pair geometric or evolutionary priors with generative, selection and mapping methods for apo-to-holo, IDP, antibody and RNA problems.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the explicit encoding of structural or evolutionary geometry in task-specific models. CrypticFlow combines Cartesian C-alpha anchors with internal-coordinate midpoints, and A2Holo runs dual-stream flow matching over language-model embeddings and 3D structure, both for apo-to-holo transitions. MANTA separates sequence-derived geometric priors from graph-Laplacian coordinate generation for IDP ensembles. FoldMapper builds structure-derived evolutionary profiles via shape-based homologue retrieval, and AbPoolRank selects antibody-antigen poses by cross-pose agreement and geometry. Infernal-GPU accelerates covariance-model search and recalibrates Rfam E-values, and TopoPPI maps interfaces into low-distortion 2D atlases. Compared with the earlier layer-wise probing of pretrained networks, the emphasis here shifts to interpretable, controllable structure generation and selection; the items do not share one algorithm.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
